KZ3 patch 1099 (SPU pass 73): lifted SPU functions use the System V calling convention on Win64 (SPU_ABI).

The Microsoft x64 convention makes xmm6-xmm15, rsi and rdi callee-saved. A lifted SPU function that uses them
saved and restored up to ten xmm registers and six general registers on every entry and exit, and since the direct
hops of patch 1096 a hot SPU loop enters and leaves one or two lifted functions per iteration (the audio mixer job's
spu_func_0000D100: 10 xmm stores, 10 xmm loads, 6 pushes and 6 pops per iteration; "entry/return" was 4.5 % of the
audio SPU thread in SPU pass 72). Under sysv_abi every xmm register is caller-saved, so chains of lifted functions
(hops, brsl calls between lifted functions) save nothing; a runtime function (Microsoft convention) that calls into
lifted code saves them once per call.
- spu_context.h: SPU_ABI = __attribute__((sysv_abi)) on Win64 GCC/clang builds (SPU_SYSV_ABI, default 1 there; build
  every TU with -DSPU_SYSV_ABI=0 for the old convention), on: tramp_fn, spu_hop_fn, spu_take_interrupt,
  spu_check_stack_reset, spu_indirect_branch, spu_ib_guess_register; spu_channels.c spu_fn, spu_run_with_halt;
  spu_drain.c spu_drain_fn and the drain loop's locals; spu_interp.h spu_lifted_fn; spu_workload.h and
  spu_lifted_job.h spu_lifted_entry_fn; the spu_run_with_halt externs; tsp_spu_func_00000A00 (weak stub and
  externs); spu_dispatch_mt.c.
- tools/spu_lifter.py: lifted functions, their declarations, the indirect-dispatch stubs, the function table and
  the guess table are SPU_ABI. C diagnoses an assignment between pointer types of different conventions, so the
  build itself checks that no lifted function is reached through a pointer of the other convention.
- GCC emits no Win64 unwind data (.pdata/.xdata) for sysv_abi functions (SPU pass 73: 11 .pdata entries for
  job_011e1180's 838 functions, against 1,470 with the Microsoft convention), and MinGW's setjmp() records its frame so that
  longjmp unwinds through RtlUnwindEx, which cannot walk such a frame: the first build stalled the K2 audio policy
  module (taskset join waiting forever). The SPU runtime's halt jump (spu_run_with_halt) and stack-reset jump
  (spu_drain.c) run no unwind handlers and now use the frameless form, SPU_SETJMP = _setjmp(buf, NULL) on MinGW
  x64 (longjmp restores the saved registers only). Stack traces of a crash inside lifted code stop at the first
  lifted frame.
Needs a relift. Linux builds are unchanged (SPU_ABI is empty off Win64). Upstream candidate.

